### What problem are you trying to solve?

MDN says "delegatesFocus default behavior is to focus the first focusable element"
and "the autofocus attribute can be specified on the element which should receive initial focus".
It should be really usefull to get the target element without having to trigger the focus.
ex : define a getter for value that reflect this element without presume the shadowRoot content.
Another ex : want to know if a custom-element is focusable? testing if shadowRoot.delegatesFocus is true is not enough. We have to know if a target element exists in this shadow dom.

### What solutions exist today?

I don't find any existing solution.

### How would you solve it?

Actually, I use this fix to ehance the shadoRoot prototype, but it would be better to have a standardize solution.

```

Object.defineProperty(ShadowRoot.prototype, 'focusTarget', {
  get: function() {
	  if(!this.delegatesFocus)
		return null;
	
	  // Chercher l'élément avec autofocus
	  const autofocusElement = this.querySelector('[autofocus]');
	  if (autofocusElement) {
		return autofocusElement;
	  }

	  // Autofocus?
	const cs = window.getComputedStyle(el, null);
	if (cs.getPropertyValue('visibility') == 'hidden' || cs.getPropertyValue('display') == 'none')
		return false;
	const focusable = '[tabindex], a[href], area[href], details, iframe, :is(button, input:not([type="hidden"]), select, textarea)';
	for(const candidate of this.querySelectorAll(focusable)) {
		if(!candidate.hasAttribute('tabindex'))
			return candidate;
		if(parseInt(candidate.getAttribute('tabindex')) >= 0)
			return candidate;
	}
	return null;
  }
});


const el = document.createElement('div');
const shadow = el.attachShadow({ mode: "open", delegatesFocus: true });
shadow.innerHTML = '<input type="text"/><slot></slot>';


console.log('el.shadowRoot', el.shadowRoot)
console.log('el.shadowRoot.delegatesFocus', el.shadowRoot.delegatesFocus)
console.log('el.shadowRoot.focusTarget', el.shadowRoot.focusTarget)
console.log('FOCUSABLE ? ', el.shadowRoot.delegatesFocus && el.shadowRoot.focusTarget)
```

